%abc-2.1
% Melody, chords and words transcribed by hand from the writer's own lead sheet,
% sources/sheetPdf.pdf (larryholdermusic.org/scores/Christ_Alive_in_Me.pdf), bar for
% bar. Bar numbers match the PDF, which counts the pickup as bar 1. The piano left
% hand and the inner voices are not transcribed (the PDF is a melody-only lead sheet).
% There is no tune.mid for this song, so nothing to cross-check; the PDF is the only
% source. Where lyrics.chordpro disagrees the PDF wins: its chords (derived from a
% machine transcription) are replaced by the PDF's, and its "Verse 4" (the last line
% sung again as a tag on the recording) is not in the PDF, so it is not written here.
% The PDF repeats bars 1-17 with three verses printed; verse 3 stops after bar 15 and
% ends on bars 18-19, written here as endings [1,2 and [3. The PDF draws an arc from
% the E ending bar 8 into bar 9, but every verse puts a new syllable on bar 9
% ("bide", "soul"), so it is read as a slur on the preceding eighths, not a tie.
% Bar 19 is a dotted half, as printed.
X:1
T:Christ Alive in Me
C:Words and Music by Lawrence Keith Holder
Z:Transcribed from the writer's lead sheet (2026)
M:4/4
L:1/8
K:D
